Now call card styles. Replace existing block from `.call-card` through `.call-address strong`. We'll add new. Also maybe adjust call-card width.

Need decide initial call-card height. `call-idle` and dialogue. CSS:
```
.call-card{...transition:...}
.call-idle{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;margin-top:11px;padding:8px 9px;border:1px dashed rgba(...,.14);background:rgba(...);}
.call-idle-mark{... bars animation}
.call-idle p{...}
.call-dialogue{display:none;margin-top:8px}
.screen-office.is-answered .call-idle{display:none}
.screen-office.is-answered .call-dialogue{display:block;animation:callIn ...}
...
.call-address{display:none}
.screen-office.call-done .call-address{display:flex;animation:...}
```
Menu hint maybe show `LINE 3`? Status changes.

`call-dot` red blink; when answered gold steady.
`call-live` status initial "INCOMING" maybe red-ish border. `.is-answered #callStatus` gold. Could use `.screen-office.is-answered .call-live`.

`call-speaker`:
```
display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:6.3;color...
call-speaking bars 3 tiny animated equalizer.
call-step margin-left auto.
```
`call-line` min-height maybe 2.6em to avoid jump; at 360 9.4px in media has font. For 390 10.5-12.5. Set min-height:3.1em. If tip long, wraps 3 lines; card grows. Fine.

`call-next`: text button align right. Ensure not full width. `.call-next` maybe appearance. Add `min-height:26px` for tap target? User wants mobile. Could make 32px high with border. Use:
```
.call-next{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin:8px 0 1px auto;min-height:28px;padding:0 2px;border-bottom:1px solid...}
```
28px small but acceptable? Better 36px. Card height. Use min-height 32. Tap target still smaller than 44, but next control. Could make full-width outline? That adds height. Use `#btnCallNext` as an inline small button but style width 100%?Maybe a full-width small ghost button with min-height 34, text uppercase. Could look good and touch. But card already has main button below. Maybe `NEXT` chip on right, 34 high. We'll use 34.

Scene button when disabled looks dim. Good.

`office-spacer` etc maybe adjust when answered. Add:
```
.screen-office.is-answered .office-head .sub{opacity:.65}
.screen-office.is-answered .office-head h1{font-size:clamp(31px,5.1vh,43px)}
```
This frees some vertical room, and card grows. At 360x640, card initial 100; answered with line ~130; no issue. Keep.

